AI-Led Development Acknowledgement

This software was written primarily by AI coding agents, directed by a human.
That is stated plainly here because it is the kind of thing this project exists
to make visible, and because you should weigh it when deciding to depend on the
code.

Every change is read by at least one human before it is merged. That single
review is the whole of the process, and it is the only assurance offered. No
claim is made that the code has been audited, formally verified, penetration
tested, or reviewed by a subject-matter expert in any domain it touches.

Two limits are worth naming, since this repository defines a format for
recording exactly these things:

  * An annotation marked `inference` records what an agent believed while
    writing the code, not an established fact. It may be wrong.

  * A passing verification claim records that a command succeeded at the moment
    a review was written. It is evidence about that moment and nothing more.
    Use `crev verify` to re-establish it.

This acknowledgement grants no rights and imposes no conditions beyond the MIT
License above; it neither adds to nor narrows that license. It restates the
disclaimer for emphasis: the software is provided "as is", without warranty of
any kind, and no author, copyright holder, contributor, or reviewer accepts any
liability for any claim, damages, or other liability arising from the software,
its use, or reliance on any statement recorded in a review within it.
